name c02m06-headhunter
timeout 300
time 1998-10-13T23:00:00Z

# DELTA FORCE (NovaLogic 1998), CAMPAIGN ONE "PERU", FILE SLOT C02M06, PLAY ORDER 6 OF 6 --
# {Headhunter}, working title "C02M06 - Capture Druglord", Objective STORM [BMS]. Unlocked by
# Masquerade, whose codebook "contained the location of the druglord's villa" [CAMP].
# Spec and provenance: mods/delta-force/doc/. Format: doc/missions/syntax.md.
#
# THE TASK [CAMP]: "Eliminate the remaining mercenaries protecting the druglord's villa, designated
# Objective Storm, and capture the druglord." M06SUBGOAL01 "Eliminate all enemy soldiers at Objective
# Storm." FAIL M06SUBFAIL01 "The enemy druglord is killed." The capture is modelled as a FAIL
# condition, not as a goal: the firefight is the goal and shooting the target loses the mission.
# THE RADIO [DLG]: "Proceed west and eliminate all hostiles in the villa." + "Do not shoot the target,
# he must be taken alive."
# THE FIELD [BMS]: 536 objects, 1458 x 980 m, IP (749.9,-381.9), enemy centroid (350.5,-307.7) =
# 406 m at 281 deg = "west". C2M6.TRN "Death & More Death", SUNSET preset (`snsgrad7`, `sun_slope 20`)
# -- confirmed by the orange sky of the manual's own screenshot [MAN p.14].
# THE CAST: 82 hostiles -> lattice pitch 132.0 m - the villa, 32 parts (types 3048-3062) on its
# measured bounding box x 201.8..315.2 / y -293.0..-178.9 = 113.5 x 114.1 m, neutral - THE DRUGLORD,
# type 5025, the only instance of that type in the whole campaign, at (260.9,-234.3), inside the villa
# - 4 Squad Member at 209 m west and 165 m north-west of the villa centre, friendly. The briefing puts
# them at 500 m; the objects are at 209 m and 165 m, and campaign.md 6 keeps both. The objects win.
# THE DRUGLORD IS DECLARED `neutral`, NOT `hostile`, and that is a decision with a consequence: team
# is a targeting class in this engine, and `kill team hostile` would otherwise demand the death of the
# one man whose death loses the mission -- two objectives that cannot both be met, which is a defect
# in the declaration and not a hard mission. Neutral plus `objective protect unit druglord` says the
# same thing the goal table says. The 2 vehicles (2009, 2012), one of them the limousine of [MAN p.14],
# are not declared: no coordinate was recorded.
#
# READING RULE (binding). campaign.md 10: a run can win every firefight and still lose, so the kill
# counter is not the verdict -- the druglord must be alive at the end. Read `protect unit druglord`
# FIRST: if it is unmet the run is lost whatever else happened. Only then read the dead-hostile count
# out of 82. The 116 m between the aim point and the druglord against a `mk82` that finishes a
# `target_soft` inside ~15 m is what makes the two compatible at all, and it is a measurement of the
# WEAPON, not of the pilot's discipline: nothing here aimed away from him. exit 3 expected.

# ---- THE NINE DISCLOSURES. Full text in c02m01-insurrection.fbm; in force here unchanged.
#   D1 no man on foot: Bravo Two flies as `f16`, 300 kt vs a 1.4 m/s walk, 150 m vs a 1.7 m eye, no
#      posture, no ground LOS, no cover - D2 the hostile soldier is a `target_soft` and cannot shoot
#      (measured: ground vs ground = 0 weapon events) - D3 the rifle has no target (gun bundles resolve
#      against aircraft only); 2 satchel charges -> 2 x `mk82` - D4 the waypoint capture radius is
#      500 m and not tunable, which is wider than four of six missions' whole ingress - D5 the N
#      hostiles are a lattice on the measured centroid at pitch sqrt(EW*NS/N); count, centroid and
#      areal density measured, arrangement reconstructed - D6 `--elev const`, flat 0 m, though fb-tiles
#      does cover Peru (629.30-688.72 m at the six box centres) - D7 the striker spawns 3 000 m out on
#      the bearing to its aim point, outside the mission box - D8 one striker is one aim point, and it
#      is also ONE RELEASE: 2 x mk82 declared, 1 fired, in every armed file - D9 date 1998-10-13 [MAN],
#      instant checked against the runner's own CLOCK line.

# MEASURED (exit 3, `--elev const`, `--threads 1/2/4` byte-identical): ONE OF EIGHTY-TWO, THE DRUGLORD
# ALIVE, AND ONE WALL DOWN.
#   t = 0.0 s    CLOCK sunElDeg -1.10 -- the .TRN sunset preset, and civil twilight to a tenth of a
#                degree. The clock is the one thing in this file that is exactly right
#   t = 11.6 s   ATTACK_RELEASE ccrp, 150.1 m, 171.5 m/s, throw 918.5 m, solution miss 22.1 m
#   t = 14.7 s   wp0 `by=capture`
#   t = 18.0 s   impact 29.9 m from the aim point. `h001` destroyed; `villa16` (NEUTRAL, a villa part
#                at 47.4 m) destroyed with it, while `villa17` at 55.0 m stood
#   t = 300.1 s  `protect unit druglord` MET -- he stands 99.8 m from the impact, and 99.8 m is the
#                whole of the discipline: nothing in this run aimed away from him
#   guns         ZERO events
#   verdict      TIMEOUT, `kill team hostile` 1 of 82, `protect unit druglord` met. Read the protect
#                first (campaign.md 10): the run did not lose. It also did not win, and it flattened
#                a piece of the villa it was sent to clear.

unit bravo2
  module f16
  team friendly
  spawn -9.30599 -76.01647 150 54.5 300
  set gear up
  set fuel_int_pct 60
  set datalink off
  set fcr_mode off
  set rwr off
  set gun_rounds 30
  set store 3 mk82
  set store 7 mk82
  set cmds_mode off
  set brief_master_arm arm
  set task attack
  set attack_mode ccrp
  wp -9.29034 -75.99423 150 300
  wp -9.27470 -75.97199 1000 300
  objective kill team hostile
  objective protect unit druglord

unit h001
  module target_soft
  team hostile
  spawn -9.29034 -75.99423 ground 134.0 0

